 Replacing d2m with the processed cp in C6 did not improve overall RMSE under the matched settings. For XGBoost, the mean paired difference was $+0.000132$~mm\,h$^{-1}$ ($+0.054\%$), with seed-t and moving-block intervals of $[-0.000776,+0.001040]$ and $[-0.001366,+0.001613]$~mm\,h$^{-1}$. For BiLSTM-Attention it was $+0.001113$~mm\,h$^{-1}$ ($+0.458\%$), with intervals of $[+0.000592,+0.001633]$ and $[+0.000095,+0.002119]$~mm\,h$^{-1}$; all five seeds had higher RMSE. The wet and upper-tail BiLSTM-Attention seed-t intervals included zero despite positive sampling intervals, so the overall result is not extended to every subset (Supplementary Table~\ref{supp-stab:r2m3_c6}). These tests support retaining the original local seven-variable configuration under the tested conditions, not the optimality of contemporaneous screening or of the predictor set.
