+
+\revminor{We additionally assessed wind speed and two large-scale atmospheric variables under matched experimental settings (Supplementary Table~\ref{supp-stab:r3c_local_additions}). Adding local wind speed, calculated from the 10-m wind components, produced no clear RMSE improvement for either XGBoost or BiLSTM-Attention. Jointly adding local 500-hPa geopotential and total-column water vapour reduced BiLSTM-Attention RMSE by 1.18\%, with both uncertainty intervals excluding zero, but produced no clear improvement for XGBoost. These findings indicate that the original candidate pool excluded potentially useful atmospheric information, although the individual contributions of geopotential and water vapour cannot be determined from the joint experiment.}
 
